<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermogenes (architect)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 3rd–2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermogenes was a Greek architect of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a>, probably from Priene or Alabanda, admired by Vitruvius as an innovator in the Ionic order. His works included the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dionysus">Dionysus</a> at Teos and the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemis">Artemis</a> Leukophryene at Magnesia on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyuk-menderes-river">Maeander</a>, which used his pseudodipteral plan. He wrote treatises on his buildings, now lost.</p></div>
